      "summary": "Perennial forage legume harvested in successive cuts. Dormancy class and acclimation affect winter survival. Heat interacts with water availability and regrowth; a stand can survive while forage production falls. Re-establishment after alfalfa can be affected by autotoxicity and shared soil-borne problems. Stand lifetime, establishment time and time between cuts are different quantities; fresh and dry forage yields must be distinguished.",
